# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A managed workflow job works like a batch job that you submit to an HPC scheduler. `run()` submits the job and returns a `Job` object immediately. Use the `Job` object for the tasks that `squeue`, the job's output file, and `scancel` cover on a cluster. The job keeps running after you close your notebook.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Job managed workflow bekerja seperti batch job yang kamu kirim ke scheduler HPC. `run()` mengirim job dan langsung mengembalikan objek `Job`. Pakai objek `Job` untuk tugas-tugas yang di cluster ditangani oleh `squeue`, file output job, dan `scancel`. Job tetap berjalan setelah kamu menutup notebook.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The examples on this page use a small workflow that reads one angle, `theta`, and fails if the angle is out of range. Upload it as described in [Deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Contoh di halaman ini memakai workflow kecil yang membaca satu sudut, `theta`, dan gagal kalau sudutnya di luar rentang. Unggah workflow itu seperti dijelaskan di [Deploy managed workflow pertamamu](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

