msgstr "Untuk menjalankan job dengan ukuran compute yang berbeda, berikan `function_size`. Lihat [Pilih ukuran untuk setiap run](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#choose-a-size-for-each-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follow a job {#follow-a-job}"
msgstr "Pantau job {#follow-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Periksa status {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Tepat setelah kamu memanggil `run()`, statusnya biasanya `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Arti |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | Job menunggu slot compute. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | Workflow sedang memulai lingkungan dengan compute profile milik job. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | Entrypoint workflow sedang berjalan. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | Entrypoint melaporkan sebuah stage dengan [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), misalnya `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Kamu membatalkan job, dan workflow sedang menghentikannya. |\n"
"| `DONE` | Entrypoint selesai dengan sukses. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | Entrypoint memunculkan error atau keluar dengan kode bukan nol. Lihat [Cari penyebab error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Kamu membatalkan job, atau job mencapai [batas 24 jam](#time-limit). |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "`DONE`, `ERROR`, dan `CANCELED` adalah status akhir, dan `job.in_terminal_state()` mengembalikan `True` untuk ketiganya. Loop status yang menunggu nilai lain, seperti `SUCCEEDED`, tidak akan pernah berhenti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Tunggu sampai job selesai {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menunggu sampai job selesai, panggil `wait_for_final_state()`. Fungsi ini mengembalikan status akhir, dan dengan `verbose=True` ia mencetak setiap perubahan status. Kalau kamu mengatur `timeout` dalam detik, `wait_for_final_state()` memunculkan `TimeoutError` saat waktu habis sebelum job selesai. Job tetap berjalan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`wait_for_final_state()` memeriksa status setelah 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, dan 32 detik, lalu setiap 60 detik, jadi ia mengetahui selesainya job singkat dalam hitungan detik dan hanya membuat sedikit request untuk job yang lama. Kalau mau memeriksa dengan interval tetap, berikan `poll_interval` dalam detik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Baca log {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Apa pun yang ditulis workflow ke standard output atau standard error masuk ke log job. Kamu bisa membacanya dengan `job.logs()` saat job berjalan, sebelum ada hasil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "Workflow mengunggah baris log baru kira-kira setiap 15 detik, dan sekali lagi saat job selesai atau dibatalkan. Tepat setelah job dimulai, `job.logs()` mengembalikan `No logs yet.`\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "Workflow menyimpan 50 MB log terbaru untuk setiap job, dan menambahkan satu baris di bagian atas yang menyatakan bahwa log sudah dipotong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menentukan apa yang dicatat workflow-mu, lihat [Tulis log](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). Untuk hanya menampilkan baris yang cocok dengan regular expression, berikan `include` ke `job.filtered_logs()`. Untuk menyembunyikan baris, berikan `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Ambil hasil {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` menunggu sampai job selesai, lalu mengembalikan nilai yang diberikan workflow ke [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Secara default, `job.result()` memeriksa status setiap 30 detik dan menunggu tanpa batas waktu. Berikan `maxwait` untuk membatasi jumlah pemeriksaan. Misalnya, `job.result(maxwait=40)` menunggu sekitar 20 menit. Untuk memeriksa sekali saja tanpa menunggu, berikan `wait=False`. Kalau `job.result()` berhenti menunggu sebelum job selesai, ia mengembalikan `{}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Periksa berapa lama setiap stage berjalan {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.events()` mencantumkan setiap perubahan status dan stage dari sebuah job beserta waktunya, jadi kamu bisa melihat berapa lama job menunggu compute dan berapa lama setiap stage berjalan:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Event memakai nama status yang tersimpan. `PENDING` adalah `INITIALIZING`, dan `SUCCEEDED` adalah `DONE`. Untuk penggunaan QPU dari sebuah run, lihat [Temukan job QPU dari sebuah run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Cari penyebab error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat workflow memunculkan exception, job berakhir dengan status `ERROR`. Misalnya, jalankan workflow dengan sudut yang ditolaknya:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Log menunjukkan traceback-nya:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Kalau workflow [melaporkan error dengan `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), baca dengan `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, dan baca pesannya dengan `job.error_message()`. Untuk job tanpa error yang dilaporkan, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` mengembalikan list kosong, dan `job.error_message()` mengembalikan `{}`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Kelola job {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Batalkan job {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Batalkan job dengan `job.cancel()`. Status berubah menjadi `CANCELING` saat workflow menghentikan job, lalu menjadi `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` mengembalikan pesan tentang job tersebut dan tentang [job QPU yang terhubung](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), yang juga coba ia batalkan. Untuk job yang sedang berjalan, workflow mengirim `SIGTERM` ke entrypoint-mu. Untuk menyimpan hasil parsial, lihat [Bersihkan saat job dibatalkan](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Kalau job sudah selesai, `job.cancel()` mengembalikan `Job already in terminal state.` dan tidak mengubah apa pun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Temukan job dari sesi baru {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Objek `Job` dan workflow hanya ada di sesi Python-mu saat ini. Setelah kamu me-restart kernel notebook, berikan ID job yang tersimpan ke `client.job()`, atau daftar job terbaru kamu dengan `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "`client.jobs()` mengembalikan 10 job terbaru kamu, dari yang paling baru. Saring dengan `function`, `status` (dari [tabel status](#check-the-status)), atau `created_after` (timestamp ISO 8601), dan telusuri halamannya dengan `limit` dan `offset`. Untuk mendaftar workflow yang sudah kamu unggah, panggil `client.list()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "Tabel [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) di IBM Quantum Platform juga mencantumkan job kamu, lengkap dengan status, compute profile, dan waktu run-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Batas waktu {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Managed workflow membatalkan job yang berjalan lebih dari 24 jam, dan job berakhir dengan status `CANCELED`. Selama run yang panjang, [simpan checkpoint ke file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) supaya kamu tidak kehilangan pekerjaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "Pemecahan masalah job {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Masalah | Penyebab |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` gagal dengan `Code: 429` dan `Active job limit reached.` | Kamu mencapai [batas job aktif](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Tunggu beberapa job selesai, atau [batalkan](#cancel-a-job) job yang tidak lagi kamu butuhkan. |\n"
"| Job tetap `QUEUED`, dan `run()` memberi peringatan `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | Job tidak akan dimulai sampai blokir pada akun, paket, atau langganan kamu dicabut. Hubungi administrator kamu. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` mengembalikan `No logs yet.` | Job sedang antre atau baru dimulai. Tunggu sekitar 15 detik. |\n"
"| `job.result()` mengembalikan `{}` | Job belum selesai, dibatalkan, atau tidak menyimpan hasil. Lihat [Simpan hasil](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` mengembalikan `{}` | Workflow memunculkan exception tanpa melaporkan error. Baca traceback dengan `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| Job berstatus `CANCELED`, padahal kamu tidak membatalkannya | Job mencapai [batas 24 jam](#time-limit). |\n"

